wasm/test — the engine's gates
==============================

Where things go
---------------
OUR test material lives HERE. Never in ../../testsuite/.

  ../../testsuite/          a git submodule pinned to the upstream
                            WebAssembly/testsuite. It is the ORACLE and is
                            read-only. Anything of ours written into it is
                            outside javelina's history, invisible to `git
                            status` at the root, and destroyed by any submodule
                            operation. Four fixture sources were lost exactly
                            that way and had to be rewritten.

  test/regress_*.wast       our own execution regressions, in .wast form, run
                            by test_wast alongside the upstream corpus.

  test/*.c                  the gates themselves (plain C, exit code is the
                            verdict — see ../../testkit/javelina_test.h).

  test/*.wat + test/*.wasm  binary fixtures and their sources.

Fixture provenance
------------------
Every .wasm fixture has a .wat source beside it, and the .wat assembles to the
committed .wasm BYTE FOR BYTE:

    ../build/water foo.wat -o /tmp/foo.wasm && cmp foo.wasm /tmp/foo.wasm

A fixture without a source needs a written reason in this file. There are
currently none.

The exceptions are the deliberately malformed binaries (bad_*.wasm): they encode
byte sequences no assembler will emit, which is the point — they exist to be
rejected. Their shape is documented at the test that consumes them.

Running one gate
----------------
    make test-one T=test_gc_los        # from wasm/
    make test-one T=test_gc_los        # from the repo root — routes by name

A failing gate prints its whole log; logs are also kept in ../build/logs/.
